  "function_translated_nl": "Lesson context: lesson_16. Let triangle PQR be a right triangle with sides PQ = 9, QR = 12. Let triangle XYZ be a right triangle with sides XY = 6. Triangle PQR is similar to triangle XYZ by AA similarity (congruent angle pairs: Q \u2245 Y). Find the length of YZ in XYZ.",
  "student_facing_prose": "A contractor is designing two similar roof trusses for a pair of buildings. The first truss, triangle PQR, is a right triangle with legs PQ = 9 feet and QR = 12 feet, meeting at the right angle Q. The second truss, triangle XYZ, is also a right triangle with a right angle at Y, and one of its legs measures XY = 6 feet.\n\nThe contractor knows that the two trusses are similar by AA similarity \u2014 specifically, the angles at Q and Y are congruent (both right angles), and the angles at P and X are also congruent. Because the trusses have the same shape, the contractor can use the proportional relationships between corresponding sides to find the unknown dimensions.\n\nWhat is the length of side YZ in the smaller truss XYZ?"
}